Now it's official --

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:07.440
the longest-running drama
in television history.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's amazing.
-Crazy.

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:10.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
Crazy, crazy.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And the longest-running
character, as well.

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:13.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've been there
from the beginning.

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:14.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
Olivia's been there
from the beginning.

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:16.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
It must be such a trip.
-I have a necklace to prove it

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you really?
-Yeah. How about that?

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:20.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow, "21!" There it is!
-21!

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-And that's not my age.

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:22.822 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:25.692
-Do you -- It is a show --
obviously, that not only

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:29.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
airs on NBC once a week,
but it's also on all the time.

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:31.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you aware of this?
-I am.

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:32.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't get away from myself
-Yeah.

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:34.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you ever flipping around
and you see your--

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:37.704 size:88% position:44%
Do you stop if you see
an old episode of "SVU?"

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:38.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Usually, not.
-Yeah.

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:42.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
-However, about a month ago,
I did and I stopped.

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:44.711
And it was so old, and I'm like,
"I don't remember that."

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:46.046 line:92%
And I said, "oh, I'll just watch

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:47.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
and remember
what episode it was."

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:50.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I sat there,
watching and watching.

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:52.585 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Half-hour went by,

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:54.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
got completely engrossed
in the show.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:57.223
Didn't remember a thing.
Didn't even know it was me

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Like, "This is a good show."

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:00.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
But it was so sad,

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:02.128 line:92%
because I could not remember

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:04.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I tried to remember
and I just couldn't.

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's -- I mean --
-That's sad.

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:08.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
I mean, you know --

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.370 line:92%
I've been doing this one now -

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:11.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
we've done this
for over five years.

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:13.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I wonder
when the time will come

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:15.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I will -- someone --
I will see someone

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:16.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
and forget that they were
a guest on the show.

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.878
-Oh.
-Do you forget guest stars ever?

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Constantly.
-Yeah.

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:21.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's bad.
-Yeah.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.216 size:78% position:39%
-But it's not so much
that I forget them.

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:25.652 size:78% position:39%
Like, the other day,
I was watching "SNL."

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:29.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there was this amazing
actor, amazing host.

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:30.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I -- We know
who we're talking about.

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:33.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's so genius.
And he was so hilarious.

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:36.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "That guy's good
That guy's great!

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:37.997 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Who is that guy?"

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:39.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's a huge star
of his own show.

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:40.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And then everyone went,

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Yeah, he was on 'SVU.'"
-Yeah, David Harbour.

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:45.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's the one!
-Yeah!

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:46.039 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:47.674
-And I couldn't remember.
And I was so embarrassed.

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:49.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I went,
"Hey, I know that guy."

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:52.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it was interesting,
'cause, David Harbour was here

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
